	(text "Battery current monitor - INA237 on an off-board 50 A / 75 mV shunt"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 25.4 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "27cefbe4-e06a-45ab-9ccc-03ae3f0406ec")
	)
	(text "U13 (INA237) measures battery current on an OFF-BOARD 50 A / 75 mV shunt (1.5 mOhm, class 0.5) in the battery NEGATIVE lead.\nMotor current never flows through this board (2.13). Shunt lugs: battery - on one side; the robot's common ground lug\n(J2 pin 1 harness lead, MDD20A VB-, charger -) on the other. Everything that returns to battery - must pass through the shunt.\nJ23: twisted 22-24 AWG Kelvin pair from the shunt's small sense screws, routed away from the motor leads.\nPin 1 = LOAD (ground-lug side) -> IN+, pin 2 = BATT (battery - side) -> IN-. Positive current = discharge.\nLow side: the sense wires sit within about 0.1 V of GND, so a chafed sense wire cannot short the battery.\nRange: board GND sits up to ~60 mV above the shunt, so IN- is about -135 mV at 50 A (limit -0.3 V).\nFull scale (ADCRANGE = 0) is +/-163.84 mV = +/-109 A. R54/R55 10 ohm + C52: input filter and dV/dt protection (SBOSA20A).\nNo ground connection at the inputs: IN+ must NOT tie to board GND on the board.\nVBUS reads +12V (after Q1, so never reversed; D13 limits it to 26 V, 85 V rating). I2C1 on PB6/PB7, address 0x40 (A0 = A1 = GND).\nALERT is open-drain, active low -> PB4 (EXTI4). Firmware: SHUNT_CAL = 819.2e6 x 4e-3 x 0.0015 = 4915 (CURRENT_LSB = 4 mA); no CHARGE register, integrate current in firmware.\nLayout: U13, R54, R55, C52 next to J23 on an edge away from U2/U5 and L1; INA_INP/INA_INN as a tight pair, no vias, no GND pour."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 33.02 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "8df3235e-b5b9-4c10-8a7c-58e102b55a43")
	)
